  "caption": "Quinn discovered padel and played five days straight. By week two the elbow was complaining, the shoulder joined in, and a back-glass sprint upset the calf.\n\nPadel niggles often come from ramping up too fast: repeated gripping, overhead smashes and quick stop-start pushes all add load. Grip size and bat weight can matter too.\n\nWhat often helps: build up gradually from around two sessions a week, check your grip size, bat and court shoes, do about 15 minutes of grip, shoulder and calf strength twice a week, and warm up with easy swings before smashing.\n\nSudden calf pain or a pop, not being able to bear weight, or a fast-swelling joint are reasons to stop and get it checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
